  "plan": {
    "goal": "Culture human proximal tubular epithelial cells (PTEC) in a microchannel under apical fluid shear reproducing the in vivo value of ~0.2 dyn/cm² (0.02 Pa).",
    "rationale": "Proximal tubular epithelial cells in vivo experience low apical shear from glomerular filtrate flow, approximately 0.2 dyn/cm² (0.02 Pa). A 400 µm × 100 µm rectangular channel (0.04 mm² cross-section) with a per-channel flow of 0.8 µL/min produces a wall shear stress of 0.02 Pa (0.2 dyn/cm²) at culture-medium viscosity (1e-3 Pa·s). Flow is laminar (Re ≈ 0.05) and the 20 mm channel gives a ~60 s residence time, appropriate for a perfused renal tubule model. Note: the physiology registry has no PTEC entry, so the 0.2 dyn/cm² target is taken from the stated physiological anchor rather than a registry range.",
